\section{Points per bin}{


With \code{score = a + b * logit} and \code{logit = alpha + sum(beta_j * woe_ij)}:
\deqn{\mathrm{points}_{ij} = b\,\beta_j\,\mathrm{woe}_{ij},\qquad
      \mathrm{base} = a + b\,\alpha.}
\code{points_style = "distributed"} spreads \code{base / k} over each
characteristic (Siddiqi, 2006, chapter 6), leaving \code{base_points = 0}. The
exact points stay in \code{points_raw}; \code{points} is the rounded version when
